        why="In C and C++, a data race is undefined behaviour you find with a sanitizer, if you're lucky. In Rust it's a compile error: the `Send` and `Sync` traits track what may cross threads, `Mutex<T>` owns the data it protects (you can't touch it without the lock), and scoped threads let workers borrow from the stack safely. Same OS threads, none of the fear.",
